# =============================================================================
# cloudflare.ini — Cloudflare DNS API credentials for certbot DNS-01.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# CREATE A SCOPED API TOKEN (NOT the Global API Key — that grants full account
# access including billing, and can't be scoped). Steps:
#
#   1. Log in: https://dash.cloudflare.com/profile/api-tokens
#   2. Click "Create Token" -> "Create Custom Token"
#   3. Token name:  certbot-deepaksharma-live
#   4. Permissions (add exactly these two rows):
#        Zone   | Zone          | Read
#        Zone   | DNS           | Edit
#      (Zone:Read is needed so certbot can look up the zone id; Zone.DNS:Edit
#      is needed to create and delete the _acme-challenge TXT records.)
#      Reference: https://certbot-dns-cloudflare.readthedocs.io/en/stable/#credentials
#   5. Zone Resources:
#        Include | Specific zone | deepaksharma.live
#      DO NOT select "All zones" — token should touch ONLY this zone.
#   6. (Optional) Client IP Address Filtering: restrict to your egress IP.
#   7. (Optional) TTL: 1 year; rotate on schedule.
#   8. "Continue to Summary" -> "Create Token" -> COPY the token (shown once).
#   9. Paste below, then:
#        chmod 600 certbot/secrets/cloudflare.ini
#
# Format: KEY = VALUE (spaces OK; newline-terminated).
# See https://certbot-dns-cloudflare.readthedocs.io/en/stable/ for the exact
# keys certbot accepts.
# =============================================================================

# Cloudflare API token (Zone:DNS:Edit on deepaksharma.live ONLY).
# Do NOT use dns_cloudflare_email / dns_cloudflare_api_key (Global API Key form)
# — that is deprecated and over-privileged.
dns_cloudflare_api_token = REPLACE_WITH_SCOPED_TOKEN
